    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="1563" n="1405" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1405"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Leishman</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1043.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of a
                        letter<anchor n="a" xml:id="d494-f1"/> from Mr. James S. McCarthy, asking if
                    the body of a person who died in the United States will be permitted to enter
                    Syria, Turkey, for burial there, the dead person having died of a disease which
                    is not contagious.</p>
                <p>You will inquire of the Turkish Government whether the burial in Syria will be
                    permitted; and if so, on what conditions.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
